# Project Criteria — Portfolio Site

## Overview
Build a single page personal portfolio website from scratch using HTML, CSS and JavaScript, deployed live on GitHub Pages with a custom dusk gradient theme.

## Core Requirements

| Requirement | Status |
|---|---|
| Build the site using only vanilla HTML, CSS and JavaScript | ✅ Met |
| Implement a dusk gradient colour scheme (purple → pink → orange) | ✅ Met |
| Create a fixed navigation bar with smooth scrolling to sections | ✅ Met |
| Build a hero section with an animated code window | ✅ Met |
| Add a typing animation for the hero greeting text | ✅ Met |
| Add scroll-triggered fade in animations for skill and project cards | ✅ Met |
| Add an active nav link that highlights based on current section | ✅ Met |
| Showcase all completed projects with GitHub links and tech tags | ✅ Met |
| Deploy live to GitHub Pages | ✅ Met |
| Push to GitHub with a professional README | ✅ Met |

## Success Scenario
Visiting KB-Dusk.github.io loads a fully styled portfolio site. The typing animation plays on load. Scrolling down triggers card fade-ins and updates the active nav link. All project GitHub links open correctly in new tabs. The site loads without errors on Chromebook and mobile.

## Evaluation
- **Design:** Dusk gradient is consistent across all elements
- **Animations:** Typing effect, fade-ins and hover transitions all work correctly
- **Navigation:** Smooth scrolling and active link highlighting work on all sections
- **Projects:** All projects are listed with correct links, descriptions and tags
